title: 'Anthill: A harvester ant colony built from the published science'
message: 'If you use this software or its parameter data, please cite it as below.'
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-20'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22819793
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22819793
    description: All versions of this software
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22819794
    description: Version 1.0.0
  # Version 1.1.0's own DOI is minted by Zenodo when the release is published, and is added
  # here afterwards. The concept DOI above always resolves to the latest version.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Adiezc/ANThill-Sim'
url: 'https://adiezc.github.io/ANThill-Sim/'
authors:
  - given-names: Adrian
    family-names: Diez Cuadrado
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7051-3055'
abstract: >-
  A browser-based, agent-based simulation of a colony of the Florida harvester ant,
  Pogonomyrmex badius, covering claustral founding, self-organised nest excavation,
  trunk-trail foraging, seed storage and germination, seasonal cycles, drought years,
  alarm on the foraging ground and annual nest relocation with the store carried between
  nests. Every modelled mechanic is tagged as documented for the species,
  generalised from another ant, or invented, and is linked to its source.
keywords:
  - agent-based model
  - myrmecology
  - Pogonomyrmex badius
  - self-organisation
  - stigmergy
  - nest architecture
